    "text": "By News Room ,\n14 hours ago Cities and counties across Arkansas are adopting or considering new restrictions on data centers as officials weigh potential investment against concerns involving electricity, water, noise and nearby property. Fayetteville, Little Rock, Pulaski County, Carroll County and Union County have each considered regulations or temporary development pauses during 2026. Local officials... Read full article\n3",
